Z||000000||Flamberge||10-07-2001||04:07 AM||||I'm a new forum-ite, but this looks like a great forum so far. I have a lot of questions, but will start out slowly...<P>First, I recently bought my third Fiero, an '88 GT (much like the one on the right of the top frame here) and have a few questions about it. <P>It is white, with "GT" trim, but it also has "Formula" written in hollow letters on the side of the doors, with multiple black pinstripes along the white (not gray or silver) base boards. Also, the top of the rear bumber, just below the breaklights, is black, and apperantly the same material as the pinstripes and Formula lettering. <P>I was under the impression until now that the "Formula" model was an in-between model, much like it is for modern Firebirds. (Base coupes, then Formulas, then Trans Am/GTs.) So why does my Fiero have both Formula "clothes" on and yet sport GT emblems, steering wheel horn cover, GT guages, etc. I should mention that the VIN# confirms its GT-ness...so why the Formula stuff? <P>That's an incredibly long-winded question, so I will ask the other ones later (like stock HP and such). Thanks all! =)<P>- Flamberge||||reg||5
Z||000001||My7Fieros||10-07-2001||05:15 AM||||First off, welcome to the forum! Ok, about your question...if it is a GT (fastback model) like the white or red on on top of this page, than the "formula" decals were just something a previous owner did for unknown reason. The Formula was 88 only, and had the basic coupe body, but w/ GT engine/drivetrane.<P>------------------<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="blue"><B><I>My 7 Fieros</FONT></FONT></B></I>||||reg||1
Z||000002||fix||10-07-2001||12:44 PM||||stock hp for the V6 is about 145 I believe.||||reg||1
Z||000003||gt boy||10-07-2001||12:54 PM||||welcome to the forum<P>------------------<BR>"it's too bad he had to run out of talent half way through the corner..."||||reg||1
Z||000004||Formula88||10-07-2001||01:24 PM||||The 88's were rated at 135HP from the factory.  That's down 5HP from 87, but no changes to the engine.  They rated it at a different rpm for emissions reasons.  Also, many Fiero V6s were dynoed back then at about 150HP or so, so the ratings don't always tell the whole story.<P>Welcome to the Forum!  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Flamberge||10-07-2001||04:26 PM||||Thanks all.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> So the Formula decals are aftermarket?<P>- Flamberge||||reg||10
