Z||000007||Flamberge||10-07-2001||11:30 PM||||Well here's a pic of my 88GT... <BR> <A HREF="http://flamberge.iwarp.com/Serra3.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://flamberge.iwarp.com/Serra3.jpg</A> <P>notice the ground effects are white and they have those pinstripes...notice the "formula" on the sides, etc... I wonder if I should take them off then.....<P>A little background incase anyone is wondering...<P>I bought a 86 SE (V-6) in Anchorage AK back in 1996. After selling it and moving back to the lower 48 (I was in the USAF) I bought an 85 SE (V-6), total beater. It was so bad I didn't even try to restore it, and since it was a four speed manual (don't laugh, but I prefer the auto,) I began looking for another one. Now I have the one in the picture. It is very nice, though now you guys/gals have me wondering what else is aftermarket? (It has fake wood veneer over the console, which I am 95% sure is aftermarket, but everything else seems legit.)<P>This forum rocks! You all should be proud to have found it so long ago, as I just discovered it last night!<P>- Flamberge||||reg||1
Z||000008||Jefrysuko||10-08-2001||12:20 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Formula88:<BR><B>The 88's were rated at 135HP from the factory.  That's down 5HP from 87, but no changes to the engine.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>They did make the change to internal balance for 88.  This wouldn't necessarily change the power output but it is a change.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Zippy_11_sig.jpg">    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif"> ||||reg||1
