Z||000010||Flamberge||10-08-2001||04:47 AM||||I checked the Vin#s on all the major components before buying the car, and the decklid doesn't match numbers, but everything else does. I need to ask the previous owner about the Forumla stuff. He was the only guy who owned it, and it was a garage car (until now, sadly) and so the interior is very nice. The steering wheel material hasn't begun to stretch or melt, etc.<P>It sure seems like more than 140 hp to me.<P>- Flamberge||||reg||1
Z||000011||grgoyl86||10-08-2001||06:16 AM||||Are we sure this is not a Formula with a GT body added to it? Check the fifth character of the VIN. A GT should be a G for a GT or an E for a Formula.<P>For further decoding, check out <A HREF="http://www.nytmare.org/fiero/vin/fierovin.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.nytmare.org/fiero/vin/fierovin.htm</A> <P><P>------------------<BR>Why do we park in driveways and drive on parkways?||||reg||5
